Portions of `recorder.py` (frame-mapping helpers `blender_frame_to_robot_frame`,
`euler_to_quaternion`, `get_root_position`, `get_root_orientation`,
`get_toe_position`) are adapted from upstream `assets/scripts/data_recording.py`.

Changes made in this fork (Open Duck Mini v2, animation-system Phase 2)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

D2  — Antenna L/R index swap FIXED. Upstream wrote `antenna.r` to canonical
      index 9 (`left_antenna`) and `antenna.l` to index 10 (`right_antenna`).
      Here index 9 = `antenna.l`, index 10 = `antenna.r`, matching
      `open_duck_anim.JOINT_ORDER_16` / `poly_reference_motion.py`. No sign is
      applied at record time (LEFT_SIGN=+1 / RIGHT_SIGN=-1 live downstream in the
      runtime PWM and the compiler's antenna_calibration), so there is no double
      inversion. See `transform_table.py`.

D3  — Hardcoded `foot_contact = [1, 1]` REPLACED. Contacts are computed from foot
      geometry (`contacts.compute_foot_contacts`), and a new top-level authoring
      key `FootContactValid` plus a `contacts_valid` panel toggle let an author
      explicitly mark non-stepping clips as contact-invalid ([0,0]) so training
      can zero the contact weight — never a silent [1,1]. See `contacts.py`,
      `export.py`.

D4  — Non-deterministic wall-clock timer recording REPLACED with an explicit
      `scene.frame_set()` loop that captures exactly one sample per frame,
      independent of playback speed. Re-recording the same scene yields
      byte-identical frames. See `recorder.DataRecorder.record`.

D11 — Baked `± np.deg2rad(10)` knee/ankle offsets REPLACED with a single explicit
      calibrated zero/sign/axis transform table (`transform_table.JOINT_TRANSFORMS`),
      one declared row per joint. A regression test pins the zero pose and a set
      of known joint angles to within 1e-6 rad.

Added
-----

* MJCF `jnt_range` Limit Rotation bone constraints (`jnt_range.py`,
  `constraints.py`), idempotently applied so out-of-range poses are unauthorable.
  Ranges sourced from
  `Open_Duck_Playground/playground/open_duck_mini_v2/xmls/open_duck_mini_v2.xml`.
* Clip-metadata panel / export options (`panels.py`): `name`, `layer_mask`,
  `blend_in_s`/`blend_out_s`, `show_blend_in_s`/`show_blend_out_s`, `loop_mode`,
  `requires_mode`, `priority` — matching the `.duckanim` schema (plan §5).
* Export path: writes the 59-float authoring JSON (unchanged training schema)
  then invokes `open_duck_anim.compiler` to produce the `.duckanim` (reused, not
  reimplemented).
* Author-time head safety-envelope warnings (`metadata.head_envelope_warnings`)
  using `open_duck_anim.envelope.DEFLECTION_LIMITS` (advisory, not a hard block).

The large `open-duck-mini.blend` binary is intentionally NOT vendored into this
repository. See README.md for how to obtain it via git-lfs.
